    "summary": "The Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments (ACME) project comprised six modular flight investigations in the Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) on the ISS: CLD Flame (Coflow Laminar Diffusion), BRE (Burning Rate Emulator), E-FIELD Flames, Flame Design, s-Flame (Spherical Diffusion), and CFI-G. ACME investigated fundamental soot processes, non-buoyant diffusion flame stabilization, and cool gas-phase flames.",
    "objectives": "Understand soot inception and oxidation in buoyancy-free laminar diffusion flames, quantify radiative heat loss, and validate non-premixed combustion kinetics models.",
    "apparatus_description": "ACME modular burner insert inside the 100-liter Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR) chamber aboard the ISS.",
